Boom_0.9.17.tar.gz

This update fixes the installation failure reported by the 'clang23' additional
check (https://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/bdr/clang23/Boom.log).  clang 23's libc++
dropped a number of transitive includes, so headers that BOOM had been getting
for free are now required explicitly.  The reported errors were

  stats/hexbin.cpp        std::lower_bound   without <algorithm>
  cpputil/ThreadTools.hpp std::atomic_bool   without <atomic>
  cpputil/parse_range.cpp back_inserter      without <iterator>

The same class of latent problem was swept for across the whole library (by
compiling with -D_LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES, and by auditing every
translation unit for std:: names whose owning header was not in the include
closure), and the missing includes were added.  Calls that had been resolving
through argument-dependent lookup are now explicitly std::-qualified.

